[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                        &lt;strong&gt;Google Eyes User Browsing Data Search in New Patent Filing (3 minute read)&lt;/strong&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;/a&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    Google has filed a patent for a system that helps users search their digital history using natural language. This system aims to make it easier for users to find previously viewed content without remembering exact keywords. While promising convenience, concerns about data privacy and user control have been raised.[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,414][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
