[2025-04-15 21:52:20,500][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,500][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    The University of Maryland Medical Center (UMMC) is being sued by current and former employees for enabling a pharmacist to conduct cyberstalking due to a lack of security practices. The pharmacist used a keylogger and installed spyware on at least 400 computers in UMMC to obtain employees&apos; usernames and passwords to access the accounts of about 80 female co-workers for nearly a decade. The hacker hacked victims&apos; cloud accounts to steal private information and used internet-connected cameras to watch the victims in their homes.[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,500][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
