[2025-04-15 21:52:20,502][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,502][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,502][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,502][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    A threat actor known as ToddyCat has exploited a vulnerability in ESET&apos;s antivirus scanner. The vulnerability could allow privileged attackers to plant a malicious DLL and execute it through the antivirus scanner. The attackers in this campaign are using a tool dubbed TCDSB, which seems to be an extension of EDRSandBlast, to alter key components of the OS and disable alerts.[\n]"
