[2025-04-15 21:52:20,512][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,513][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;/a&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,513][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,513][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,513][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,513][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    A hacker breached the GitLab repos of the Europcar car rental company and stole source code for the mobile apps and personal information belonging to up to 200K customers. The threat actordiscovered 9,000 SQL files, which include customers&apos; names and email addresses, and 269 .env files. Europcar has confirmed the breach but has not provided more information.[\n]"
