[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Java is one of the most widely-used open source ecosystems in the enterprise. It is also a &lt;a href=&quot;https://tracking.tldrnewsletter.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.chainguard.dev%2Funchained%2Fannouncing-chainguard-libraries-guarded-java-language-dependencies-built-from-source%3Futm_source=TLDRinfosec%26utm_medium=email%26utm_content=email-ad/1/01000195dce3cb04-ff7d9d86-f278-4f1c-bb1e-f8d0da35abc8-000000/seFmJJyshi9oNKW6iNSM5o9WUEz5IL4BRzWSgOwtySM=398&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;very common target for supply chain attacks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; targeting builds or dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;li&gt;For example, the MavenGate attack in Jan 2024 involved attackers compromising abandoned Maven Central domains to hijack critical java projects like Gradle.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;li&gt;Because public package registries only apply minimal vetting for their hosted artifacts and optimize for publisher convenience, they sacrifice secure and standardized enterprise consumption.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;li&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://tracking.tldrnewsletter.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.chainguard.dev%2Flibraries%3Futm_source=TLDRinfosec%26utm_medium=email%26utm_content=email-ad/3/01000195dce3cb04-ff7d9d86-f278-4f1c-bb1e-f8d0da35abc8-000000/am5A6uViVrBk-N5AjoJCZS6QwEqXd7L5Qnqi3MaAwUA=398&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;newly-introduced Chainguard Libraries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; delivers one standardized source for developers to safely consume language libraries, without compromising supply chain security.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;li&gt;As an added benefit, it removes the toil associated with package curation and minimizes friction by preserving existing developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;/ul&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:20,663][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://tracking.tldrnewsletter.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.chainguard.dev%2Funchained%2Fannouncing-chainguard-libraries-guarded-java-language-dependencies-built-from-source%3Futm_source=TLDRinfosec%26utm_medium=email%26utm_content=email-ad/2/01000195dce3cb04-ff7d9d86-f278-4f1c-bb1e-f8d0da35abc8-000000/I2AHrtjANGc2G78TtF8o-XXhAKjhPYMb9T0LhSBQNCA=398&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;[0xe2][0x86][0x92] Learn more about Libraries on the Chainguard blog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;[\n]"
