[2025-04-15 21:52:20,664][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    Google has fixed a high-severity Chrome zero-day vulnerability that allowed malicious users to escape the browser sandbox. Researchers from Kaspersky reported this vulnerability, which they described as an [0xe2][0x80][0x9c]incorrect handle provided in unspecified circumstances in Mojo on Windows.[0xe2][0x80][0x9d] Attackers are actively exploiting this vulnerability to infect targets with sophisticated malware used for espionage. A similar zero-day vulnerability was also recently disclosed and patched in Firefox.[\n]"
