[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "  &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDHSCISA/2020/06/3486054/05152023-gov-delivery-banner-copy_original.png&quot; alt=&quot;Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA)&quot; title=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;600&quot; height=&quot;100&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "  &lt;p&gt;You are subscribed to Cybersecurity Advisories for Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency. This information has recently been updated and is now available.&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;div class=&quot;rss_item&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 2em;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;div class=&quot;rss_title&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: bold; font-size: 120%; margin: 0 0 0.3em; padding: 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/04/11/fortinet-releases-advisory-new-post-exploitation-technique-known-vulnerabilities&quot;&gt;Fortinet Releases Advisory on New Post-Exploitation Technique for Known Vulnerabilities&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;div class=&quot;rss_pub_date&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 90%; font-style: italic; color: #666666; margin: 0 0 0.3em; padding: 0;&quot;&gt;04/11/2025 10:00 AM EDT&lt;/div&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;div class=&quot;rss_description&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0.3em; padding: 0;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,113][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;p&gt;Fortinet is aware of a threat actor creating a malicious file from previously exploited Fortinet RCE vulnerabilities within FortiOS and FortiGate products. This malicious file could enable read-only access to files on the devices[0xe2][0x80][0x99] file system, which may include configurations.[0xc2][0xa0]&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;p&gt;See the following resource for more information:&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;ul&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fortinet.com/blog/psirt-blogs/analysis-of-threat-actor-activity&quot; title=&quot;Analysis of Threat Actor Activity&quot;&gt;Analysis of Threat Actor Activity | Fortinet Blog&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;/ul&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;p&gt;CISA encourages administrators to review Fortinet[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s advisory and:&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;ul&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;li&gt;Upgrade to FortiOS versions 7.6.2, 7.4.7, 7.2.11, 7.0.17, 6.4.16 to remove the malicious file and prevent re-compromise.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;li&gt;Review the configuration of all in-scope devices.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;li&gt;Reset potentially exposed credentials.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;li&gt;As a work-around mitigation until the patch is applied, consider disabling SSL-VPN functionality, as exploitation of the file requires the SSL-VPN to be enabled.&lt;/li&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;/ul&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;p&gt;Organizations should report incidents and anomalous activity to CISA[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s 24/7 Operations Center at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Report@cisa.gov&quot; title=&quot;Report to CISA&quot;&gt;Report@cisa.gov&lt;/a&gt; or (888) 282-0870.[0xc2][0xa0]&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;p&gt;For more mitigation information: &lt;a href=&quot;https://community.fortinet.com/t5/FortiGate/Technical-Tip-Recommended-steps-to-execute-in-case-of-a/ta-p/230694&quot; title=&quot;Recommended Steps to Execute&quot;&gt;Recommended steps to execute in case of a... - Fortinet Community&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:52:21,114][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-19 << "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;This product is provided subject to this[0xc2][0xa0]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cisa.gov/notification&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; title=&quot;Notification&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Notification&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;[0xc2][0xa0]and this[0xc2][0xa0]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cisa.gov/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; title=&quot;Privacy &amp;amp; Use&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Privacy &amp;amp; Use&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;[0xc2][0xa0]policy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;[\n]"
