e execution and potential cluster takeover. They estimate ~40% of cloud environments are vulnerable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The vulnerabilities stem from improper input sanitization, allowing attackers to inject arbitrary directives in the NGINX configurations, as well as gain RCE via uploading a malicious shared library using NGINX client body buffering and loading it via an injected &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;ssl_engine&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; directive during configuration testing. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt; [0xf0][0x9f][0x92][0xa1]&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; The exploit chain for configuration injection [0xe2][0x86][0x92] RCE is pretty rad &lt;/span&gt;[0xf0][0x9f][0xa4][0x98]&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Wiz bringing that IDF/8200 energy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;table role=&quot;none&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=&quot;transparent&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent;padding:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;table role=&quot;none&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpad